{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionBarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionBarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.transfer_not_entailed_by_toda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.transfer_not_entailed_by_toda","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L62-L75","doc":"**Toda barrier (sorry-free): the transfer is NOT entailed by Toda.** A\nconcrete world satisfies Toda (`fpEqSharpP → pEqNp`) yet **falsifies** the\ntransfer — it has `P = NP` *together with* counting-hardness `¬(FP=#P)`. So\nno argument that uses only the counting↔decision implication which is\nactually a theorem can establish the transfer: `#P`-hardness alone cannot\nseparate `P` from `NP`. This is the propositional skeleton of Toda's\nrelativization barrier; the oracle strengthening is cited, not formalized. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.Transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.Transfer","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L54-L58","doc":"**The counting→decision transfer** as a predicate on a world: counting\nhardness (`¬ FP=#P`) forces the decision separation (`¬ P=NP`). This is the\nframework's open hypothesis — the *converse* of `toda`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.fpNe_of_pNe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.fpNe_of_pNe","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**The direction that HOLDS: `P ≠ NP ⟹ FP ≠ #P`** — the contrapositive of\nToda, discharged sorry-free from the field. A genuine *decision* separation\nforces a *counting* separation; this is the only implication between the two\nthat the literature supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.toda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.toda","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L43-L43","doc":"**Toda's implication** (`#P ⊆ FP ⟹ PH ⊆ P^{#P} = P ⟹ P = NP`): if exact\ncounting collapses to `FP`, so does the decision hierarchy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.fpEqSharpP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.fpEqSharpP","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L40-L40","doc":"`FP = #P` (exact counting collapses to poly-time function computation)\nholds in this world. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.pEqNp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.pEqNp","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L37-L37","doc":"`P = NP` holds in this world. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.CountingDecisionWorld","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingDecisionBarrier.lean#L33-L43","doc":"An abstract world carrying the two separation propositions and the ONE\nimplication between them that is a theorem: Toda's `FP = #P ⟹ P = NP`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}